# Build context of the images whose context is the repository root (srl-provider, intent-translator;
# versions.lock.yaml firstPartyImages). scripts/lib/image_build.sh honours this file when it computes
# an image's contentHash, and docker when it builds.
#
# The kustomizations a build WRITES its content-hash tag into are outputs of the build, never its
# inputs: were they hashed, writing the tag would change the tree's hash, so a re-run would rebuild
# under a new tag every time and no running workload would ever carry the tree's hash
# (make verify-compat). The provider and the first-party allocation authority run the same tag.
deploy/agentic-netops/kustomization.yaml
deploy/allocation/kustomization.yaml

# Not build inputs of any repository-root image (docker/Dockerfile.srl-provider copies go.mod, go.sum,
# api/, cmd/, controllers/, internal/, pkg/ and versions.lock.yaml only). tests/ in particular holds
# tests/gate/observed/*.json, which the capability gate REWRITES at GateReady — after AppsReady built
# the image — so hashing it made every gate run change the tree's hash: a re-run rebuilt and rolled
# the provider, and make verify-compat failed on a freshly provisioned lab (AD-82 decision
# 2026-09-21-build-context, docs/decisions/live-findings.md). docs/ and specs/ are text only.
tests/
docs/
specs/

# Every kustomization a build writes a tag into, not only the provider's own (T152 r9: provisioning
# the tier rewrote deploy/agents/kustomization.yaml, the provider's hash moved under the running
# provider and the control-plane-only make verify-compat failed). And every other directory neither
# repository-root Dockerfile COPYs — the agents, the UI, the manifests, the scripts — so that no
# edit or build output outside the Go sources and the lock can move a running image off the tree's
# hash (docs/decisions/live-findings.md 2026-09-28-root-context).
deploy/
agents/
ui/
scripts/
examples/
lab/
config/
hack/
testautomation/
.github/
TUTORIAL.md
README.md
